  "conclusion": "All three arms refuse with phase=5/reason=3/Need=1, no quality result. With feedforward disabled, Rs remains 20M while input 2 grows from L=1 to L=89; after its timing error reaches 1.43ms (within SyncTolerance=20ms), the amplitude controller lowers Rs geometrically 20M→12.001M→7.202M→5M while measured peak remains around 1e-5..3e-5 against an initial 0.06999. The next input then grows to L=65 and has invalid peaks. Thus feedforward is not necessary for Rs to reach its floor, and disabling it does not restore convergence; it changes when Rs falls and which active input reaches the floor. This is a single diagnostic condition, not proof of impossibility."
